// Microsoft Defender for Identity raises dedicated alerts when Kerberos TGTs show golden-ticket anomalies
// (nonexistent account referenced, ticket lifetime/encryption anomalies indicating a forged TGT minted from krbtgt).
// Tuned to reduce false positives: matches only Golden-Ticket-specific alert names (drops the generic "Ticket
// anomaly" phrase, which also fires for unrelated Kerberos ticket issues) and drops Informational/Low severity
// alerts, which are typically benign anomalies rather than confirmed forged tickets.
SecurityAlert
| where TimeGenerated > ago(14d)
| where ProviderName in ("Azure Advanced Threat Protection", "Microsoft Defender for Identity")
| where AlertName has_any ("Golden Ticket", "Suspected Golden Ticket")
| where AlertSeverity in ("High", "Medium")
| extend Entities = parse_json(Entities)
| project TimeGenerated, AlertName, AlertSeverity, Description, Entities, CompromisedEntity, VendorOriginalId
| sort by TimeGenerated desc